<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwKA"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwKQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A8">Cell group A8</h2>
<p id="mwKg">Group A8 is a small group of dopaminergic cells in rodents<sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dahlstrom"},"2":{"wt":"Fuxe"},"3":{"wt":"1964"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6" id="mwKw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">]</span></span></a></sup> and primates.<sup about="#mwt22" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwLw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">]</span></span></a></sup> It is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Midbrain_reticular_formation" title="Midbrain reticular formation" id="mwMw">midbrain reticular formation</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Dorsolateral" title="Dorsolateral" class="mw-redirect" id="mwNA">dorsolateral</a> to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Substantia_nigra" title="Substantia nigra" id="mwNQ">substantia nigra</a> at the level of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Red_nucleus" title="Red nucleus" id="mwNg">red nucleus</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Caudally" title="Caudally" class="mw-redirect" id="mwNw">caudally</a>. In the mouse it is identified with the retrorubral field as defined by classical stains.<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paxinos"},"2":{"wt":"Franklin"},"3":{"wt":"2001"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7" id="mwOA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwPA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A9">Cell group A9</h2>
<p id="mwPQ">Group A9 is the most densely packed group of dopaminergic cells, and is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ventrolateral" title="Ventrolateral" class="mw-redirect" id="mwPg">ventrolateral</a> midbrain of rodents<sup about="#mwt28" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964_6-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dahlstrom"},"2":{"wt":"Fuxe"},"3":{"wt":"1964"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6" id="mwPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">]</span></span></a></sup> and primates.<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwQw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRg">]</span></span></a></sup> It is for the most part identical with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Pars_compacta" title="Pars compacta" id="mwRw">pars compacta</a> of the substantia nigra as seen from the accumulation of neuromelanin pigment in the midbrain of healthy, adult humans.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt34" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cn","href":"./Template:Cn"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2022"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwSA"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_February_2022" about="#mwt34"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt34" id="mwSQ"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (February 2022)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwSg"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A10">Cell group A10</h2>
<p id="mwSw">Group A10 is the largest group of dopaminergic cells in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ventral" title="Ventral" class="mw-redirect" id="mwTA">ventral</a> midbrain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Tegmentum" title="Tegmentum" id="mwTQ">tegmentum</a> of rodents<sup about="#mwt35" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964_6-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dahlstrom"},"2":{"wt":"Fuxe"},"3":{"wt":"1964"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6" id="mwTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and primates.<sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The cells are located for the most part in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ventral_tegmental_area" title="Ventral tegmental area" id="mwVg">ventral tegmental area</a>, the linear nucleus and, in primates, the part of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Central_gray" title="Central gray" class="mw-redirect" id="mwVw">central gray</a> of the midbrain located between the left and right <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Oculomotor_nucleus" title="Oculomotor nucleus" id="mwWA">oculomotor nuclear</a> complexes.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt41" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cn","href":"./Template:Cn"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2022"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwWQ"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_February_2022" about="#mwt41"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt41" id="mwWg"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (February 2022)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwWw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A11">Cell group A11</h2>
<p id="mwXA">Group A11 is a small group of dopaminergic cells located in the posterior <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Periventricular_nucleus" title="Periventricular nucleus" id="mwXQ">periventricular nucleus</a> and the intermediate periventricular nucleus of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hypothalamus" title="Hypothalamus" id="mwXg">hypothalamus</a> in the macaque.<sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">]</span></span></a></sup> In the rat, small numbers of cells assigned to this group are also found in the posterior nucleus of hypothalamus, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Mammillary_body" title="Mammillary body" id="mwYw">supramammillary</a> area and the reuniens nucleus.<sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964_6-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dahlstrom"},"2":{"wt":"Fuxe"},"3":{"wt":"1964"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6" id="mwZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">]</span></span></a></sup> Dopaminergic cells in A11 may be important in the modulation of auditory processing.<sup about="#mwt48" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENevueFelix_IIPortfors2016_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENevueFelix IIPortfors2016"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENevueFelix_IIPortfors2016-8"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Nevue"},"2":{"wt":"Felix II"},"3":{"wt":"Portfors"},"4":{"wt":"2016"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTENevueFelix_IIPortfors2016-8" id="mwaA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwag">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwbA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A12">Cell group A12</h2>
<p id="mwbQ">Group A12 is a small group of cells in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Arcuate_nucleus" title="Arcuate nucleus" class="mw-redirect" id="mwbg">arcuate nucleus</a> of the hypothalamus in primates.<sup about="#mwt51" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">]</span></span></a></sup> In the rat a few cells belonging to this group are also seen in the anteroventral portion of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Paraventricular_nucleus_of_hypothalamus" title="Paraventricular nucleus of hypothalamus" class="mw-redirect" id="mwcw">paraventricular nucleus of the hypothalamus</a>.<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964_6-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dahlstrom"},"2":{"wt":"Fuxe"},"3":{"wt":"1964"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDahlstromFuxe1964-6" id="mwdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mweA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A13">Cell group A13</h2>
<p id="mweQ">Group A13 is distributed in clusters that, in the primate, are ventral and medial to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Mammillothalamic_tract" title="Mammillothalamic tract" id="mweg">mammillothalamic tract</a> of the hypothalamus; a few extend into the reuniens nucleus of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Thalamus" title="Thalamus" id="mwew">thalamus</a>.<sup about="#mwt57" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwfA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">]</span></span></a></sup> In the mouse, A13 is located ventral to the mammillothalamic tract of the thalamus in the zona incerta.<sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001_7-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paxinos"},"2":{"wt":"Franklin"},"3":{"wt":"2001"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7" id="mwgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwhA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A14">Cell group A14</h2>
<p id="mwhQ">Group A14 consists of a few cells observed in and near the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Preoptic_area" title="Preoptic area" id="mwhg">preoptic</a> periventricular nucleus of the primate.<sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">]</span></span></a></sup> In the mouse, cells in the anterodorsal preoptic nucleus are assigned to this group.<sup about="#mwt66" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001_7-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Paxinos"},"2":{"wt":"Franklin"},"3":{"wt":"2001"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPaxinosFranklin2001-7" id="mwiw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjQ">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwjw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A15">Cell group A15</h2>
<p id="mwkA">Group A15 exists in a few species, such as sheep, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Immunoreactivity" title="Immunoreactivity" class="mw-redirect" id="mwkQ">immunoreactive</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Tyrosine_hydroxylase" title="Tyrosine hydroxylase" id="mwkg">tyrosine hydroxylase</a>, a precursor of dopamine, in many other species including rodents and primates. It is located in ventral and dorsal components within the preoptic periventricular nucleus and adjacent parts of the anterior hypothalamic region. It is continuous caudally with the dopaminergic group A14.<sup about="#mwt69" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTETillet1994_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTETillet1994"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTETillet1994-9"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Tillet"},"2":{"wt":"1994"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTETillet1994-9" id="mwkw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlQ">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwlw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_A16">Cell group A16</h2>
<p id="mwmA">Group A16 is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Olfactory_bulb" title="Olfactory bulb" id="mwmQ">olfactory bulb</a> of vertebrates, including rodents and primates.<sup about="#mwt72" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESmeetsReiner1994_3-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESmeetsReiner1994"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESmeetsReiner1994-3"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Smeets"},"2":{"wt":"Reiner"},"3":{"wt":"1994"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTESmeetsReiner1994-3" id="mwmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnA">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwng"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Cell_group_Aaq">Cell group Aaq</h2>
<p id="mwnw">Group Aaq is a sparse group of cells located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Anatomical_terms_of_location#Directional_terms" title="Anatomical terms of location" id="mwoA">rostral half</a> of the central gray of the midbrain in primates. It is more prominent in the squirrel monkey (Saimiri) than the macaque.<sup about="#mwt75" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983_4-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek Jr1983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Felten"},"2":{"wt":"Sladek Jr"},"3":{"wt":"1983"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFeltenSladek_Jr1983-4" id="mwoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwog"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwow">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwpQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Telencephalic_group">Telencephalic group</h2>
<p id="mwpg">This group is a population of cells immunoreactive for dopamine and tyrosine hydroxylase that are broadly distributed in the rostral <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Forebrain" title="Forebrain" id="mwpw">forebrain</a>, including such structures as: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Substantia_innominata" title="Substantia innominata" id="mwqA">substantia innominata</a>, diagonal band, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Olfactory_tubercle" title="Olfactory tubercle" id="mwqQ">olfactory tubercle</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Prepyriform_area" title="Prepyriform area" id="mwqg">prepyriform area</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Striatum" title="Striatum" id="mwqw">striatum</a> (at levels rostral to the anterior <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Commissure" title="Commissure" id="mwrA">commissure</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Claustrum" title="Claustrum" id="mwrQ">claustrum</a>, and deep <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Cortex_(anatomy)" title="Cortex (anatomy)" id="mwrg">cortical</a> layers of all <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Gyri" title="Gyri" class="mw-redirect" id="mwrw">gyri</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Frontal_lobe" title="Frontal lobe" id="mwsA">frontal lobe</a> rostral to the head of the caudate nucleus; the cells are also numerous in intervening <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./White_matter" title="White matter" id="mwsQ">white matter</a>, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./External_capsule" title="External capsule" id="mwsg">external capsule</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Extreme_capsule" title="Extreme capsule" id="mwsw">extreme capsule</a> and frontal white matter. They are found in the rodent, the macaque and the human.<sup about="#mwt78" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDubach1994_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEDubach1994"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDubach1994-5"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfnp","href":"./Template:Sfnp"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dubach"},"2":{"wt":"1994"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Dopaminergic_cell_groups#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDubach1994-5" id="mwtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwuA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="See_also">See also</h2>
